hing on him i don't mean to beat this  to death but of course he's the  quarterback the super bowl team and  everybody talks about him but like what  do you take away from the year that  you'll try to preach to him is you know  the the banner theme for 2020 football  season  mine to jimmy is just that you're just  getting started no last year was your  first year playing quarterback for a  whole season like you've never had a  longer than a three-game stretch and  last year you got 16. and look how good  you did look how far we got and oh my  god we almost got all the way but that's  not the finished product and that's how  i feel about everything i feel about  myself i feel about our team like guys  that's we didn't just almost get there  we're still going and you have to get  better and what i like about our team is  when i'm talking about jimmy  how can he not get better he's played  one season  and that's just the starting point you  look at some of our receivers some of  our d linemen like we got guys who  almost played good enough and we almost  coached good enough last year first to  win a super bowl and that that's hard  it's a hard pill to swallow that it  wasn't enough what's really cool is when  i look at our team  and i'm not making stuff up  no one's at their peak individually our  guys should get better like our guys  they our guys can get better our  receivers can our d-line can our  quarterback can or bro we got we got  guys who can get better and that's  what's exciting and with jimmy i know  everyone thinks he's been the league so  long because he's gotten a second  contract and everything um but  quarterbacks with his ability um they  get better the more they play and the  more situations they're in and that's  the key for jimmy it's just to know that  and keep doing it  kyle shanahan with chris sims on jimmy  garoppolo and look  the narratives that emerged about jimmy  garoppolo last year resulted from a  couple of things first of all he had  some unfortunate throws in the  divisional round playoffs against the  vikings he threw three passes that  should have been intercepted by eric  kendricks one was the other two weren't  after the last one  the 49ers shifted to all run they stayed  in all run  through the divisional round through the  conference championship round creating a  question as to whether or not jimmy g  was going to be bob griese in super bowl  54 throwing the ball maybe eight or nine  times at most and then he came out and  threw it more and there was a time  before the chiefs turned it around  people were saying hey jimmy g is going  to be the mvp of the game shireen and  then it all came down to having the  opportunity to hit emmanuel sanders with  the game on the line he missed him and  that's kind of where we are like i i  they got a great team around jimmy g  i've yet to see anything that makes me  say  this is a top  top tier nfl quarterback and when you  have the opportunity to make that  championship throw and you miss it  that's your chance to bust through and  it's pass fail and it doesn't come very  often it came for jared goff last year  and it didn't happen it came for jimmy  garoppolo this year and it didn't happen  and until he makes a throw like that in  the super bowl that that ghost is going  to linger for  yeah i think i was just going to start  out i think i like jimmy g more than you  do mike and i do see him going to get  into that top tier of quarterbacks  you're right he still has that and he  has to get past that i understand that  was that last point that that kyle  shanahan made and and i was going to  make that same point is this is a young  older guy and that he's played six  seasons but he hasn't played six seasons  he hasn't played very many games  last year was his first 16 game season  as kyle shanahan pointed out the more  you play the better you get so this is a  young guy who knows the offense who  knows what he needs to do he knows how  to read defenses now i think we're going  to see jimmy g have one of the top two  or three  quarterbacks in the league this year i  really do i think he's going to have a  great season i think the 49ers are going  to have a great season on paper they  look terrific  if he can stay healthy i think this is a  team that you're going to look to be in  the nfc championship game if not advance  the super bowl again and give him  another opportunity to make those throws  that he didn't make in the fourth  quarter of the super bowl this year  and regardless of anything that kyle  shanahan said yesterday about jimmy  garoppolo jimmy g is on notice he knows  he's on notice he's addressed it himself  the idea that they evaluated tom brady  and kyle shanahan talks about that with  chris sims talks about why shanahan took  it head-on and told jimmy g about it but  they looked into the possibility of  bringing tom brady home to the team that  he grew up rooting for and there was  some thought that that was brady's first  choice and at the end of the day jimmy g  ended up being the 49ers first choice  but the message is not that anyone needs  to hear this if you're not getting it  done in the nfl they're going to find  somebody else and it applies at every  position and they are in the years of  the jimmy garoppolo contract where it's  very easy to move on if that's what they  choose to do minimal cap hit minimal  financial obligation they could move on  after 2020 they could have moved on  after 2019 with a very minimal cap hit  like 4.2 million dollars so uh hey  maybe that is the thing shireen that  nudges him to the next level that that  kind of backhanded  threat to his status if you want to be  the year to your quarterback of this  team and you want to hold this job the  way brady held it for as long as he did  in new england you got to step up and  you got to get it done and and we'll see  if that's the impetus for him to do it  he did so many great things in the  regular season he had over 